---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
const title = "What Is Text Readability? WCAG Ratios Explained - Toolkit Lab";
const description = "What colour contrast ratio means, the WCAG 4.5:1 and 7:1 guidelines for text, and how to check text colours before publishing a website.";
---
<Base title={title} description={description} path="/guides/what-is-colour-contrast-and-why-it-matters">
  <aside class="ad-rail" aria-label="Advertisement"><div class="ad-slot ad-slot-rail"></div></aside>
  <div class="wrap article">
    <p class="note"><a href="/guides">Guides</a> / Accessibility</p>
    <h1>What Is Text Readability? WCAG Ratios Explained</h1>
    <p class="lead">Text is easier to read when it is clearly darker or lighter than the background behind it. This guide explains how that difference is measured, and why it matters for older readers and anyone with weaker eyesight.</p>
    <div class="ad-slot" aria-label="Advertisement"></div>
<h2>Why contrast matters</h2>
<p>If text and its background are close in brightness, the words blur together. This is hard for everyone, but especially for older readers and people with weaker eyesight. Good contrast makes a page easier and more comfortable to read.</p>
<h2>How it is measured</h2>
<p>Contrast is given as a ratio from 1:1 (no difference) to 21:1 (black on white). The higher the number, the easier the text is to read.</p>
<h2>The guidelines</h2>
<ul>
<li>Ordinary text should reach at least 4.5:1.</li>
<li>Large text, such as 18 point, needs at least 3:1.</li>
</ul>
<h2>A common mistake</h2>
<p>Light grey text on white can look neat but be hard to read. If in doubt, make the text darker.</p>
      <section class="worked">
        <h2>Worked example</h2>
        <p>Grey text in the colour #767676 on a white background has a contrast of about 4.5 to 1. That just meets the minimum for ordinary text. A lighter grey, #999999, is about 2.8 to 1, which is too faint.</p>
      </section>
      <section class="faq-list">
        <h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>
        <details><summary>Does this apply to decoration?</summary><p>No. Pure decoration and logos do not need to be easy to read.</p></details>
        <details><summary>What counts as large text?</summary><p>Text of 18 point or bigger, or bold text of 14 point or bigger. Large text has a lower minimum.</p></details>
        <details><summary>Do I need to check dark mode too?</summary><p>Yes. Dark backgrounds need their own check, because the same colours can look different on them.</p></details>
      </section>
